      ],
      "words": 59
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I’d spent five years guarding it, like grief gave me ownership over every memory made here. But",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 16581
        },
        {
          "text": "“You don’t have to let Willow Creek recreate James’s festival.” He continued. “Make it your own.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17235
        },
        {
          "text": "“You’re never going to recreate what it was.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17552
        },
        {
          "text": "That should have hurt. Instead, it felt almost relieving",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17595
        }
